**Suggested fix:**

```css
.shell {
  min-height: 100vh;
  max-height: 100vh;
  overflow: hidden;
}
```

Then make the recipe display independently scrollable:

```css
.recipe-panel {
  max-height: calc(100vh - 220px);
  overflow-y: auto;
}
```

This keeps the overall `.shell` inside the viewport while allowing long recipe details to scroll inside the right-hand recipe section.

For smaller screens, I recommend allowing normal page scrolling because the layout stacks vertically:

```css
@media (max-width: 1080px) {
  .shell {
    max-height: none;
    overflow: visible;
  }

  .recipe-panel {
    max-height: none;
    overflow: visible;
  }
}
```

